  "note_crew": "Flight deck: floor y 31, pilot seat backs z -207..-203, cushions y ~40, glare shield y 50 at z -222, roof y 64-68. The An-12 eyes (y 59 / 63.8) were at or inside the roof; the pilots look through the windscreen (whose lower edge is ~16 deg above a coaming-level eye) at y 58.5, 5 px under the roof; the engineer and navigator/radio operator sit behind at y 60. The source's cargo ramp is modelled open (airdrop configuration) and stays so: the lower rear fuselage is not in the model.",
